### Content summary

- **Purpose** — AI judgment on focal path (hero → proof → depth) via scale, contrast, grouping, and CTA weight; complements deterministic CTA/heading rules.
- **Passing / failing signals** — Tied to real KS classes from `components/components.py` and `css/forgesdlc-theme.css`: `product-landing-title`, `landing-hero-kicker`, `landing-hero-tagline`, `btn-forge`, `btn-cyan-outline`, `landing-hero-secondary-link`, `section-label`, `card-amber`, `breathe-link`, `breathe-static`, `landing-forge-visual`, etc.
- **Before example** — Failing hero with competing `h2`/`h1`/`h2`, four CTAs, competing `card-amber` stat card, three equal `card-amber` outcome tiles.
- **After example** — Single `product-landing-title`, primary + outline CTA + secondary link, diagram in `landing-hero-visual`, one accented outcome + two `breathe-static` siblings, mechanism band at lower weight.
- **Evidence and remediation** — Squint test, DOM capture, 7-step fix order; promotion via `AI.RULE_DISCOVERY.CANDIDATE_DETERMINISTIC_RULE` (removed non-registry `AI.VISUAL.HIERARCHY_CONFIDENCE` cross-links per batch convention).

